+1.1 On an overlap with (s_j=s_i g_{ij}), [F3] gives (F_j=\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}F_i). Since (B) is invariant, (B(F_j\wedge F_j)=B(F_i\wedge F_i)); the curvature-polynomial evaluation [F4] is therefore the global four-form (\frac{1}{8\pi^2}B(F\wedge F)), independent of the chosen local section. The polynomial (P_B(Z)=B(Z,Z)/(8\pi^2)) is homogeneous, quadratic, and (G)-invariant, so [F4] also identifies this form with its Chern–Weil representative. [given, F3, F4, algebra]
