## Definition

Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let (X) be a connected, compact, oriented, finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable smooth four-manifold without boundary, with a supplied Riemannian metric. Let (Gsubseteq U(V,h)) be a compact non-Abelian matrix Lie group in its specified global form, let (pi:P	o X) be a smooth right principal (G)-bundle in a specified bundle sector, and let (omega) be a supplied smooth principal connection. Let (B:mathfrak g	imesmathfrak g	omathbb R) be a positive-definite symmetric bilinear form invariant under (operatorname{Ad}(G)). For local sections (s_i:U_i	o P), set (A_i=s_i^*omega) and (F_i=dA_i+	frac12[A_iwedge A_i]). If (F_i=sum_a e_a F_i^a) in a finite basis of (mathfrak g), define (B(F_iwedge F_i):=sum_{a,b}B(e_a,e_b)F_i^awedge F_i^b); this expression is independent of the basis. The **trace-normalized topological charge** is

$$
q_B(P,omega):=rac{1}{8\pi^2}int_X B(F_i\wedge F_i).
$$

The local four-forms agree on overlaps, so the integrand is global. The number (q_B(P,omega)) is independent of the supplied connection. For a general compact matrix group and invariant (B), it is a real characteristic number; no integrality is asserted. In the special case (G=SU(2)) in its defining representation on (mathbb C^2), with (B(X,Y)=-\operatorname{tr}_2(XY)), the associated Hermitian bundle (E=P\times_{SU(2)}\mathbb C^2) has

$$
q_B(P,\omega)=-\langle c_2(E),[X]\rangle\in\mathbb Z,
$$

where (c_2(E)\in H^4(X;\mathbb Z)) is the integral second Chern class and ([X]\in H_4(X;\mathbb Z)) is the orientation fundamental class. This sign is fixed by the library convention (c(E,\nabla)=\det(I-\Omega_\nabla/(2\pi i))).

The Hodge operator ( *_g) on two-forms is characterized by α\wedge *_gβ=\langle\alpha,\beta\rangle_g\,d\operatorname{vol}_g) and acts componentwise on γ-valued forms. Set (F_i^+=(F_i+*_gF_i)/2) and (F_i^-=(F_i-*_gF_i)/2). The self-dual sector consists of connections with (F_i^-=0), equivalently (F_i=*_gF_i); the anti-self-dual (ASD) sector consists of connections with (F_i^+=0), equivalently (F_i=-*_gF_i). These conditions are independent of the local section.

## Definition references

