## Statement

Assume full Axiom of Choice and the hypotheses of [[def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector]] on a compact, connected, oriented Riemannian four-manifold without boundary. For the same invariant positive-definite form $B$, let $g>0$ be a real scalar and define the Euclidean Yang–Mills functional by

$$
S_B(P,\omega):=\frac{1}{g^2}\int_X B(F_i\wedge *_g F_i),
$$

where the local integrands patch to a global four-form. Then

$$
S_B(P,\omega)\geq \frac{8\pi^2}{g^2}\,|q_B(P,\omega)|.
$$

Equality holds exactly in these cases: if $q_B>0$, then $F_i=*_gF_i$; if $q_B<0$, then $F_i=-*_gF_i$; if $q_B=0$, then $F_i=0$. Every self-dual or anti-self-dual supplied connection satisfies the source-free Euclidean Yang–Mills equation $D_{A_i}(*_gF_i)=0$, where $D_{A_i}\eta=d\eta+[A_i\wedge\eta]$. The statement asserts neither existence nor uniqueness of a connection in any charge sector.

## Statement references

[Belavin–Polyakov–Schwartz–Tyupkin, printed pp. 85–86](https://strings.itp.ac.ru/Papers/belavin1975.pdf)

[Tong, Lecture 1 §1.1.1](https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/tasi/instanton.pdf)

