+Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $S^4=\{z\in\mathbb R^5:|z|=1\}$ have its unit round metric. Denote by $p_\infty$ the point omitted by the north stereographic chart and by $p_0$ the point with north-chart coordinates $x=0$. Orient $S^4$ so that north-chart coordinates $x=(x^1,x^2,x^3,x^4)$ satisfy $dx^1\wedge dx^2\wedge dx^3\wedge dx^4>0$. Set $r^2=\sum_{\mu=1}^4(x^\mu)^2$. The metric in the north chart is $4(1+r^2)^{-2}\sum_{\mu=1}^4(dx^\mu)^2$. Let $U_N=S^4\setminus\{p_\infty\}$ carry coordinate $x$, and $U_S=S^4\setminus\{p_0\}$ carry coordinate $y=x/r^2$; the metric in the south chart is $4(1+|y|^2)^{-2}\sum_{\mu=1}^4(dy^\mu)^2$.
+
+Define $SU(2)=\{U\in M_2(\mathbb C):U^*U=I,\det U=1\}$. Write $\epsilon_{123}=1$ and let
+
+$$
+\sigma_1=\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix},\qquad
+\sigma_2=\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\i&0\end{pmatrix},\qquad
+\sigma_3=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&-1\end{pmatrix},\qquad
+T_a=-\frac{i}{2}\sigma_a.
+$$
+
+The $T_a$ are traceless anti-Hermitian generators. Set $B(X,Y)=-\operatorname{tr}_2(XY)$. Define antisymmetric symbols by $\eta_{aij}=\epsilon_{aij}$, $\eta_{ai4}=\delta_{ai}$, $\bar\eta_{aij}=-\epsilon_{aij}$, and $\bar\eta_{ai4}=\delta_{ai}$ for spatial indices $i,j\in\{1,2,3\}$, where $\delta_{ai}$ is the Kronecker delta; extend them antisymmetrically in the last two indices. For a scale parameter $\rho>0$, define $u(x)=(x^4I-i x^j\sigma_j)/r\in SU(2)$ on $U_N\cap U_S$. Glue the trivial right $SU(2)$-bundles on $U_N$ and $U_S$ by the local-section transition $s_S=s_Nu^{-1}$, and define their local connection potentials by
+
+$$
+A_N=\frac{2\eta_{a\mu\nu}x^\nu}{r^2+\rho^2}T_a\,dx^\mu,\qquad
+A_S=-\frac{2\rho^2\bar\eta_{a\mu\nu}y^\nu}{1+\rho^2|y|^2}T_a\,dy^\mu.
+$$
+
+On the overlap these obey $A_S=\operatorname{Ad}_u A_N+u\,d(u^{-1})$, so they define a smooth principal connection on the glued bundle. Let $F$ be its global curvature, with chart representatives $F_N$ and $F_S$. In the north chart its curvature, written $F_N=\tfrac12F^N_{\mu\nu}dx^\mu\wedge dx^\nu$, has components
+
+$$
+F^N_{\mu\nu}=-\frac{4\rho^2}{(r^2+\rho^2)^2}\eta_{a\mu\nu}T_a.
+$$
+
+Let $*_X$ be the Hodge star characterized on two-forms by $\alpha\wedge *_X\beta=\langle\alpha,\beta\rangle_X\,d\operatorname{vol}_X$, acting componentwise on the Lie-algebra coefficients. This curvature is self-dual, meaning $F_N=*_XF_N$. With $B$ as fixed above, define the charge by $q_B=(8\pi^2)^{-1}\int_{S^4}B(F\wedge F)$ and, for any real $g>0$, define the action by $S_B(g)=g^{-2}\int_{S^4}B(F\wedge *_XF)$. Then $q_B=1$, $S_B(g)=8\pi^2/g^2<\infty$, and the action saturates the self-dual bound. This is one explicit Belavin–Polyakov–Schwartz–Tyupkin (BPST) charge-one connection; no uniqueness or moduli classification is asserted.
